@prefix ag: <http://example.org/agora#> .

#  This agent's PRIVATE beliefs — and there is only one block, because it composed only one
#  capability.
#
#  What is absent is the point. No ag:Bidding block: no endowment, no target, no band, no
#  price. This agent holds no stake, so it has no opinion about what a reading MEANS — it
#  records the number and announces it. Compare world/society/beliefs-fern.ttl, which is the
#  same agent in a world that gives it something to want.

##  ag:Subscribing — the interval it asks its board to keep
#
#  Both figures sit on the constitutional floor (ag:minSleepS 10, in
#  capabilities/perception/ontology.ttl), because a board being brought up should be seen
#  often. They are EQUAL, and honestly so: with no stake there is no trouble to watch harder
#  for, so there is one rate. A plant agent's two differ because it has a band to be near.
ag:fern_agent
    ag:fastSleepS 10 ;
    ag:slowSleepS 10 ;
    ag:readingGraceS 45 .     # it still decides what is too old to be current

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see agora/metrics.py.
ag:fern_agent ag:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  Self-review — how often at the very least, and how much room it gives itself.
#   Omit ag:reviewIntervalS and it never revises anything: its beliefs stay exactly what
#   genesis wrote. The commitment is the SELF constraint — narrower than the constitution's
#   10..900 — so the figure above is a first pick rather than a floor, and this says how far
#   the agent will let itself wander from it. See decisions/a-belief-is-a-pick-within-a-range.
ag:fern_agent ag:reviewIntervalS 300 .
ag:fern_agent ag:commits [ ag:onTerm ag:slowSleepS ; ag:notBelow 10 ; ag:notAbove 900 ] .
